negative control for every structural floor is stated over a population the project would accept as correct, so no passing condition requires a known defect to be present; A repair that removes a meaningless edge or node is distinguishable at the gate from an erosion that removes recorded work, without a hand edit to the declaration; The graph audit's four legacy remediation codes can be executed to zero with every block-enforcement assurance gate still passing, proven by running them; Placeholder-inclusive node counts remain available as a diagnostic measurement and are explicitly marked as unsuitable as a ratchet basis"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"explainable-graph"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"A structural floor is denominated over the population the project intends to preserve, so executing a prescribed repair can never fail it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Governance is only worth running if its verdict tracks the thing it claims to protect. A floor that requires broken data inverts that: the safest tracker state is the one the gate rejects."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Blocks the entire legacy graph hygiene programme: three of pm-hnc9w7's four acceptance criteria cannot be satisfied without failing a block-enforcement gate."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Node and edge floors are denominated over real recorded items and real stored edges; placeholder-inclusive counts remain a diagnostic and are never a ratchet basis."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"Demonstrated live this session, not argued: executing the audit's own prescribed remediation drove a block-enforcement gate from pass to fail."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-96h7"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":95},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1jzupz","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:30:00.326Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-96h7","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:30:00.326Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-9gzr4r","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:30:00.326Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-hnc9w7","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:30:00.326Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-o2kc","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:30:00.326Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-w7ccmv","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:30:00.326Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bc6c7b75da19a25d73e2caf2cdf704d165304aa089e6fd414c5a69f84f47f2d6","item_hash_version":2,"message":"File the node-floor instance of the ratchet-direction defect, proved by executing the audit's prescribed remediation"}
{"ts":"2026-08-13T08:31:34.425Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7ebf2cca0e1c37e7b3d988ef","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-hnc9w7","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.229","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Measured this session, in order\n\nStarting state: `pm graph audit` reported 11 findings across four legacy codes; `pm assurance run tracker-context-quality --trigger ci` reported `verdict: pass`. Graph profile: 2,458 nodes, of which 3 were assembly-materialized placeholders for dangling references (`missing_nodes: 3`), and 12,116 edges.\n\nExecuted exactly the remediation the audit prescribes, on three of its four codes:\n\n- 8 duplicated `child` spellings collapsed onto the canonical `parent` edge each child already stored (`legacy_duplicate_edge` 8 to 0);\n- 3 dangling references removed: one dependency row to an item that does not exist, and two legacy free-text `blocked_by` scalars that were never item ids (`missing_reference_terminal` 3 to 0);\n- 98 retired `no-active-blocker` sentinel scalars cleared (`legacy_no_blocker_sentinel` 98 to 0).\n\nResulting state: 8 findings, all of one remaining code. Graph profile: 2,455 nodes, `missing_nodes: 0`, 12,105 edges. `pm assurance run tracker-context-quality --trigger ci` now reports `verdict: block`, `exit_code: 1`, on `graph-nodes-floor`: observed 2455, floor 2456, distance -1, enforcement `block`.\n\nThe three nodes that disappeared are exactly the three placeholders. The corpus of real recorded items did not change.\n\n## The declaration says so in its own words\n\n`pm assurance show measurement graph-nodes` describes its source as \"All indexed graph nodes including missing placeholders\" and reads `profile.nodes` from the audit.\n\n`pm assurance show assertion graph-nodes-floor` carries `floor: 2456` and this negative control:\n\n```\nnegative_control:\n  cases[2]{observed,expected}:\n    2456,pass\n    2455,fail\n```\n\nThere are 2,455 real items. The negative control therefore states that a corpus containing every recorded item and zero dangling references must fail. The floor is satisfiable only while at least one reference points at an item that does not exist.\n\n## Why this is a second instance, not a restatement\n\npm-9gzr4r owns the edge-count floor being denominated over a population that includes the edges the graph itself calls redundant. That is an argument about redundancy. This is a different measurement (`graph-nodes`), a different assertion owner (pm-o2kc), and a different mechanism: placeholder materialization during assembly, which is a deliberate feature so bounded traversals can explain absent work rather than silently dropping it. The feature is correct. Ratcheting a floor over its output is what is wrong.\n\n## The edge floor blocks the fourth code as well\n\n`graph-edges-floor` is 12103 with `enforcement: block`; observed is 12105, so headroom is 2 edges. The remaining legacy code is 8 terminal ordering cycles across 49 items, whose root cause is 26 holders that each store a legacy scalar `blocked_by: X` together with a contradicting structured row `X, blocks`. Removing those 26 inverted rows takes edges to 12,079 and fails the floor by 24.\n\nSo all four of pm-hnc9w7's remediation criteria are individually blocked by a total-count floor. The finding-count ceilings in the same registry behave correctly and reward the same cleanup: `graph-finding-legacy-duplicate-edge` (ceiling 8), `legacy-no-blocker-sentinel` (98), `missing-reference-terminal` (3) all moved to 0 and still pass. Two families of declarations in one registry disagree about whether cleanup is progress.\n\n## Boundary\n\nThe fix is the denominator, not the numbers. Raising or lowering a floor by hand is the erosion this class is supposed to detect, so the repair must make removal-of-meaningless and removal-of-meaningful structurally distinguishable at the gate."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T08:31:34.425Z"}],"before_hash":"bc6c7b75da19a25d73e2caf2cdf704d165304aa089e6fd414c5a69f84f47f2d6","after_hash":"1734eee06ea02be3e9eab0e5473dd5a909be4e3bb0379065c7dc8c91f9a6603e","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Record the measured sequence and the exact declaration text"}
